        a: "For a routine Dallas trip, BRO is the simplest option. For literally any other destination — especially Mexico — the drive to HRL or MFE is almost always worth it given how much wider their route networks are.",
      },
    ],
  },
  LRD: {
    intro: "More trade crosses the World Trade Bridge in Laredo than through almost any other land port in the country — by trade value, Laredo regularly ranks among the busiest ports in the entire US, ahead of most major seaports. That trucking and logistics economy, not tourism, is what fills seats at Laredo International, where American and United connect business travelers to DFW and Houston on a schedule built around weekday commerce rather than weekend leisure.",
    stats: [
      { label: "Annual passengers", value: "400K+" },
      { label: "Primary connections", value: "DFW, IAH" },
      { label: "Airlines at LRD", value: "2+" },
      { label: "Known for", value: "Busiest US-Mexico trade port" },
    ],
    routes: [
      { destination: "Dallas / DFW", typical: "$100–$200", errorFare: "$49–$89" },
      { destination: "Houston (IAH)", typical: "$100–$180", errorFare: "$49–$79" },
      { destination: "San Antonio (SAT)", typical: "2.5 hr drive", errorFare: "12+ airlines" },
      { destination: "International (via hubs)", typical: "Hub connection", errorFare: "Via DFW/IAH" },
    ],
    tips: [
      "LRD's fares track the trade and logistics business calendar — weekday morning departures serve corporate accounts and stay pricier, while weekend and evening flights have more room to drop.",
      "American and United's corporate travel contracts dominate demand here. Booking outside Monday–Friday morning windows is the most reliable way to find a leisure-friendly fare.",
      "Award programs sometimes zone LRD with San Antonio or Austin, making points redemptions from Laredo occasionally as cheap as flying from either larger market.",
      "For anything beyond DFW or Houston, the 2.5-hour drive to San Antonio adds 12+ airlines and over 50 nonstop destinations LRD simply doesn't have.",
    ],
    faqs: [
      {
        q: "Why is Laredo's airport so business-travel focused?",
        a: "Laredo's World Trade Bridge handles an enormous share of US-Mexico trade — by some measures more than any other land port in the country — and that logistics and trucking economy drives consistent weekday business travel between LRD and the American and United hubs at DFW and Houston.",
      },
      {
        q: "What are the cheapest flights from Laredo, Texas?",
        a: "Dallas and Houston routes run $49–89 during flash sales, mostly on flights outside the Monday–Friday business-travel windows. For more options, San Antonio (2.5 hours away) opens up over 50 nonstop destinations LRD doesn't serve.",
      },
      {
        q: "When is the best time to book a flight out of Laredo?",
        a: "September and January tend to be cheapest. Within any given week, weekend departures or Friday afternoon/Sunday leisure-pattern flights usually undercut the weekday-morning business fares that dominate LRD's schedule.",
      },
      {
        q: "Is it worth driving from Laredo to San Antonio for a flight?",
        a: "For international trips or anything beyond Dallas/Houston, yes — SAT's route network dwarfs LRD's two-airline setup. For routine business travel to either Texas hub, LRD's convenience usually outweighs the 2.5-hour drive.",
      },
    ],
  },
  ABI: {
    intro: "Dyess Air Force Base, home to the Air Force's B-1B Lancer bomber fleet, sits right next to Abilene Regional — giving this West-Central Texas airport a steady undercurrent of military travel alongside the university traffic from Abilene Christian and Hardin-Simmons. Downtown, Abilene markets itself as the Storybook Capital of America for its sculpture trail of fairy-tale characters, which has nothing to do with flight prices but tells you this is a city that knows how to make a small market interesting. The airport itself runs almost entirely on a single American Eagle connection to DFW.",
    stats: [
      { label: "Annual passengers", value: "300K+" },
      { label: "Primary connection", value: "DFW via AA Eagle" },
      { label: "Drive time to DFW", value: "3 hrs" },
      { label: "Anchored by", value: "Dyess AFB (B-1B Lancer)" },
    ],
    routes: [
      { destination: "Dallas / DFW", typical: "$80–$180", errorFare: "$39–$79" },
      { destination: "International (via DFW)", typical: "Hub connection", errorFare: "DFW zone" },
      { destination: "Austin (AUS)", typical: "3 hr drive", errorFare: "75+ destinations" },
      { destination: "Dallas (DFW)", typical: "3 hr drive", errorFare: "260+ destinations" },
    ],
    tips: [
      "Dyess AFB personnel should check Space-A availability before booking commercial — it's frequently the cheaper option for eligible military travelers, though seats aren't guaranteed.",
      "Abilene Christian and Hardin-Simmons create predictable demand spikes at graduation (May), move-in (August), and Thanksgiving. Book outside those windows for the best ABI fares.",
      "Award programs frequently zone ABI identically to DFW — the same miles redeemed from Abilene can reach the same international destinations as flying out of Dallas.",
      "ABI's three-hour drive to either DFW or Austin is long enough that it's only worth it for major international trips, not routine domestic travel — price both before committing to the drive.",
    ],
    faqs: [
      {
        q: "Does Dyess Air Force Base affect flights from Abilene?",
        a: "Dyess AFB, home to the B-1B Lancer bomber fleet, adds a steady stream of military travel to ABI's passenger base alongside the university traffic from Abilene Christian and Hardin-Simmons. Eligible military personnel should compare Space-A flight availability against commercial ABI fares before booking.",
      },
      {
        q: "What are the cheapest flights from Abilene, Texas?",
        a: "ABI's only direct route is to DFW, typically $39–79 during flash sales. Beyond that, you're pricing a 3-hour drive to Dallas or Austin against whatever the DFW connection costs — often the drive only pays off for international trips.",
      },
      {
        q: "When does Abilene see the biggest flight price spikes?",
        a: "University graduation in May, move-in week in August, and Thanksgiving travel all push ABI fares higher on an already-limited daily schedule. January, February, and September are typically the cheapest months.",
      },
      {
        q: "Is ABI's nickname 'Storybook Capital of America' related to its airport?",
        a: "No — it refers to a downtown sculpture trail of fairy-tale characters and has no bearing on flight schedules or pricing. It's local color, not a factor in how American Eagle prices the DFW route.",
      },
    ],
  },
};

const airportContent = AIRPORT_CONTENT[airportData.code] ?? null;

const airportMeta = AIRPORT_META[airportData.code] ?? {
  title: `${airportData.code} Cheap Flights: Live Deals`,
  description: `Find live and archived flight deals from ${airportData.city}, including route-specific fare drops and Texas airport alerts from ${airportData.code}.`,
};
const title = `${airportMeta.title} | Texas Cheap Flights`;
const description = airportMeta.description;

// JSON-LD for the airport page
const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "WebPage",
      "@id": `${Astro.url.href}#webpage`,
      "url": Astro.url.href,
      "name": title,
      "description": description,
      "breadcrumb": {
        "@id": `${Astro.url.href}#breadcrumb`
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "@id": `${Astro.url.href}#breadcrumb`,
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 1,
          "name": "Texas Cheap Flights",
          "item": "https://texascheapflights.com/"
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 2,
          "name": `Deals from ${airportData.city}`,
          "item": Astro.url.href
        }
      ]
    },
    ...(airportContent?.faqs?.length ? [{
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": airportContent.faqs.map(faq => ({
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": faq.q,
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": faq.a }
      }))
    }] : [])
  ]
};
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>{title}</title>
  <meta name="description" content={description} />
  <link rel="canonical" href={`https://texascheapflights.com/deals/from/${airport?.toLowerCase()}`} />
  
  <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
  <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
  <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
  <meta property="og:image" content="https://texascheapflights.com/og-image.png" />
  
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />
  
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Satoshi:wght@400;500;700;900&family=Outfit:wght@400;500;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
</head>
<body class="text-tcf-ink min-h-screen">

  <GlobalNav activePage="past-deals" />

  <main class="pt-32 pb-24 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      
      <header class="mb-16">
        <span class="text-tcf-gold-deep font-bold text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] mb-4 inline-block">Regional Airport Scout</span>
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-black mb-6 leading-tight">
          Cheap Flights from <br/><span class="text-gold italic">{airportData.city} ({airportData.code})</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-tcf-ink-muted max-w-2xl font-body leading-relaxed">
          We monitor every major airline and award program departing from {airportData.city}. No more generic alerts for DFW when you're flying out of {airportData.code}.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-tcf-ink-muted">
          <span class="rounded-full border border-tcf-gold/20 bg-tcf-gold/5 px-3 py-2 text-tcf-gold-deep">Airport-specific radar</span>
          <span>{dealList.length} archived alerts</span>
          {lastUpdated && <span>Last alert {lastUpdated.toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: 'short', day: 'numeric', year: 'numeric' })}</span>}
        </div>
      </header>

      {dealList.length > 0 ? (
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-black text-tcf-ink uppercase tracking-widest mb-8">Recent Alerts from {airportData.code}</h2>
          <div class="grid gap-4">
            {dealList.map((deal) => (
              <a href={`/deal/${deal.id}`} class="block liquid-glass p-6 rounded-2xl border border-tcf-ink/10 hover:border-tcf-gold/30 transition-all duration-300 group no-underline text-inherit">
                <div class="flex justify-between items-center">
                  <div>
                    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
                        <span class={`text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-widest px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full border ${deal.score >= 8 ? 'text-tcf-gold-deep border-tcf-gold/30 bg-tcf-gold/5' : 'text-tcf-ink-muted border-tcf-ink/10'}`}>
                            Score: {deal.score}/10
                        </span>
                        <span class="text-[10px] text-tcf-ink-muted">{new Date(deal.sent_at).toLocaleDateString()}</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="text-xl font-black text-tcf-ink group-hover:text-tcf-gold-deep transition-colors">{deal.origin} → {deal.destination}</div>
                    <div class="text-xs text-tcf-ink-muted mt-1">{deal.airline} · {deal.travel_dates}</div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="text-right">
                    <div class="text-2xl font-black text-tcf-ink">{deal.price ? `$${deal.price}` : 'Points'}</div>
                    <div class="text-[10px] text-tcf-ink-muted uppercase tracking-widest mt-1">Roundtrip</div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </a>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      ) : (
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <!-- Scout Status Card -->
          <div class="p-8 rounded-[2rem] liquid-glass border border-tcf-gold/20">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
              <span class="relative flex h-3 w-3">
                <span class="animate-ping absolute inline-flex h-full w-full rounded-full bg-tcf-gold opacity-75"></span>
                <span class="relative inline-flex rounded-full h-3 w-3 bg-tcf-gold"></span>
              </span>
              <span class="text-xs font-black text-tcf-gold-deep uppercase tracking-[0.2em]">AI Scout Active — {airportData.code}</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-black text-tcf-ink mb-3">No archived deals yet — Scout is watching.</h3>
            <p class="text-tcf-ink-muted leading-relaxed font-body max-w-xl">
              Our AI hasn't flagged a sendable deal from {airportData.city} yet, but the radar is live. Error fares and award arbitrage windows from {airportData.code} tend to be brief — most close within 2–4 hours. Subscribers get the alert the moment one surfaces.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- What We Watch For -->
          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
            <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-tcf-ink/5 border border-tcf-ink/10">
              <p class="text-xs font-black text-tcf-gold-deep uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">Error Fares</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-tcf-ink-muted leading-relaxed font-body">Airline pricing glitches that can slip through for hours before the carrier pulls them. Legal to book, often honored, but never guaranteed.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-tcf-ink/5 border border-tcf-ink/10">
              <p class="text-xs font-black text-tcf-aviation-blue uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">Zone Awards</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-tcf-ink-muted leading-relaxed font-body">Award programs price by zone, not distance. {airportData.code} often costs the same points as DFW or IAH to the same destination.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-tcf-ink/5 border border-tcf-ink/10">
              <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest mb-3" style="color: var(--tcf-success)">Sweet Spots</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-tcf-ink-muted leading-relaxed font-body">Partner award pricing that's mispriced relative to cash. Rare but high-value — often 70–80% below retail.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- CTA -->
          <div class="p-8 rounded-[2rem] bg-tcf-gold/5 border border-tcf-gold/20 flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-6">
            <div>
              <p class="font-black text-tcf-ink text-lg mb-1">Get the first alert when a deal drops from {airportData.city}.</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-tcf-ink-muted font-body">No spam. One alert per deal. Unsubscribe in one click.</p>
            </div>
              <a href="/#waitlist" data-tcf-event="cta_clicked" data-tcf-location="airport_hub" data-tcf-label={`Alert Me for ${airportData.code}`} data-airport={airportData.code} class="btn-primary whitespace-nowrap no-underline" style="background: var(--tcf-gold); color: #050a14; font-weight: 900; padding: 0.75rem 2rem; border-radius: 9999px; font-size: 0.875rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;">
              Alert Me for {airportData.code}
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      )}

      <!-- Rich Airport Content Section -->
      <section class="mt-24 pt-24 border-t border-tcf-ink/10">
        {airportContent ? (
          <div class="space-y-20">

            <!-- Intro + Stats -->
            <div>
              <p class="text-tcf-ink-muted text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-3xl font-body mb-10">{airportContent.intro}</p>
              <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
                {airportContent.stats.map(stat => (
                  <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-tcf-ink/5 border border-tcf-ink/10 text-center">
                    <div class="text-2xl font-black text-tcf-ink">{stat.value}</div>
                    <div class="text-xs text-tcf-ink-muted mt-1 uppercase tracking-wider">{stat.label}</div>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Historical Deal Ranges -->
            <div>
              <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-tcf-ink mb-2">Typical vs. Error Fare Prices from {airportData.city}</h2>
              <p class="text-sm text-tcf-ink-muted mb-6 font-body">Historical ranges based on observed deals. Error fares close within 2–6 hours — subscribe to get notified instantly.</p>
              <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-tcf-ink/10">
                <table class="w-full text-sm min-w-[500px]">
                  <thead>
                    <tr class="bg-tcf-ink/5 border-b border-tcf-ink/10">
                      <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs text-tcf-ink-muted font-bold uppercase tracking-wider">Destination</th>
                      <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs text-tcf-ink-muted font-bold uppercase tracking-wider">Typical Price</th>
                      <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider" style="color: var(--tcf-gold-deep);">Error Fare Range</th>
                    </tr>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody>
                    {airportContent.routes.map((route, i) => (
                      <tr class={`border-b border-tcf-ink/10 ${i % 2 === 0 ? '' : 'bg-tcf-ink/5'}`}>
                        <td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-tcf-ink">{route.destination}</td>
                        <td class="px-4 py-3 text-tcf-ink-muted line-through text-sm">{route.typical}</td>
                        <td class="px-4 py-3 font-black" style="color: var(--tcf-gold-deep);">{route.errorFare}</td>
                      </tr>
                    ))}
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Pro Tips -->
            <div>
              <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-tcf-ink mb-6">Pro Tips for Finding Cheap Flights from {airportData.city}</h2>
              <div class="space-y-3">
                {airportContent.tips.map((tip, i) => (
                  <div class="flex gap-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-tcf-ink/5 border border-tcf-ink/10">
                    <span class="font-black text-sm mt-0.5 shrink-0" style="color: var(--tcf-gold-deep);">{i + 1}.</span>
                    <p class="text-tcf-ink-muted text-sm leading-relaxed font-body">{tip}</p>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- FAQ Section -->
            <div>
              <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-tcf-ink mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions — Cheap Flights from {airportData.city}</h2>
              <div class="space-y-4">
                {airportContent.faqs.map(faq => (
                  <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-tcf-ink/5 border border-tcf-ink/10">
                    <h3 class="font-black text-tcf-ink mb-2 text-base">{faq.q}</h3>
                    <p class="text-tcf-ink-muted text-sm leading-relaxed font-body">{faq.a}</p>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>
        ) : (
          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12">
            <article class="prose prose-sm max-w-none">
              <h3 class="text-tcf-ink font-black text-lg mb-4">Why monitor {airportData.city}?</h3>
              <p class="text-tcf-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
                Departing from {airportData.code} often means you're limited to regional connections or high-priced positioning flights. However, award programs often price {airportData.code} to international destinations the same as DFW or IAH. This creates arbitrage windows where you can fly from your backyard for the same price as a major airport.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article class="prose prose-sm max-w-none">
              <h3 class="text-tcf-ink font-black text-lg mb-4">Best Strategy for {airportData.code}</h3>
              <p class="text-tcf-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
                Our AI Scout specifically looks for Zone-Based redemptions and error fares that propagate to regional TX feeders. For {airportData.city} travelers, we recommend keeping a stash of transferable points to lock in these windows before they vanish.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
        )}
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <footer class="py-20 border-t border-tcf-ink/10 text-center text-xs text-tcf-ink-muted">
    <p>© 2026 Texas Cheap Flights · <a href="/past-deals" class="text-tcf-ink-muted hover:text-tcf-ink transition-colors no-underline">Back to All Deals</a></p>
  </footer>

</body>
</html>
